---
/**
 * The central states, with the three campuses that hold GP-STOR storage picked
 * out from the wider region the project serves.
 *
 * This started as a Plotly export loaded as an external image file, which meant
 * page CSS could not reach it: it shipped an opaque white plate that read as the only
 * light card on a dark page, and it filled six states in one identical blue, so
 * the map claimed a six-state footprint the project does not have.
 *
 * Inlined here for the same reason the hero network and the access-paths
 * diagram are inline -- the site's theme is a manual toggle, not the OS
 * setting, so only a `.dark` class on the page can be trusted to say which
 * palette to draw. Amber marks the three funded sites, matching the colour both
 * other graphics reserve for GP-STOR itself; the rest of the region sits behind
 * them in neutral. Coordinates are rounded to a tenth of a viewBox unit, which
 * is well under a pixel at the size this ever renders.
 */
---

<svg class="csm" viewBox="48 -2 415 447" fill="none" role="img" aria-labelledby="csm-title">
  <title id="csm-title">
    Map of the central United States. South Dakota, Nebraska, and Missouri, the three campuses
    holding GP-STOR storage, are marked in amber; Kansas, Oklahoma, and Arkansas are shown in
    neutral as part of the wider region served.
  </title>

